---
const rows = [
  ["The cook tasted the soup.", "Action: the cook did the tasting."],
  ["The soup tasted salty.", "Linking: tasted joins soup to salty."],
  ["She looked at the clock.", "Action: she used her eyes."],
  ["She looked tired.", "Linking: looked joins her to tired."]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Verbs - Actions and states</h1>
  <p>
    A <strong>verb</strong> tells us about an action, occurrence or state. In “The fox <strong>jumped</strong>,”
    it shows an action. In “The fox <strong>is</strong> hungry,” <em>is</em> links the subject to a
    description.
  </p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>Action or linking?</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Sentence</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Job of the verb</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          rows.map(([sentence, job]) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{sentence}</td>
              <td>{job}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  <p>
    Action verbs include visible actions (<strong>run, lift, build</strong>) and less visible ones
    (<strong>think, remember</strong>). Forms of <em>be</em> (<strong>am, is, are, was, were</strong>) often
    link a subject to a description: “The soup <strong>smells</strong> delicious”; “He
    <strong>became</strong> a doctor.”
  </p>
  <p>
    A verb can contain more than one word. In “They <strong>were running</strong>,” <em>were</em> is a
    helping verb and <em>running</em> is the main verb. Other groups include <strong>has finished</strong> and
    <strong>might arrive</strong>. When you are asked for the whole verb, include the helping verb.
  </p>
  <p class="try-it">
    <strong>Try it.</strong> Is <em>felt</em> an action or a linking verb in “I felt the rough stone” and
    “The stone felt rough”? Find the whole verb in “The children were laughing.”
  </p>
  <div class="trap-card trap-compact">
    <section class="trap">
      <h2>Don’t drop the helping verb</h2>
      <p>
        The children running.
        <span class="mark mark-no" aria-label="Incorrect">✕</span>
      </p>
      <p>
        The children <strong>were running</strong>.
        <span class="mark mark-yes" aria-label="Correct">✓</span>
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="trap">
      <h2>After a linking verb, use an adjective</h2>
      <p>
        The soup tastes wonderfully.
        <span class="mark mark-no" aria-label="Incorrect">✕</span>
      </p>
      <p>
        The soup tastes <strong>wonderful</strong>.
        <span class="mark mark-yes" aria-label="Correct">✓</span>
        <em>Tastes</em> links soup to a description.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
